Keeps `logs/` present in a fresh clone.

Django's LOGGING config declares a RotatingFileHandler at logs/security.log
(backend/settings/base.py). RotatingFileHandler opens its file when logging is
configured — during django.setup() — so if this directory is missing, EVERY
management command dies before it does anything:

    ValueError: Unable to configure handler 'security_file'
    FileNotFoundError: .../logs/security.log

.gitignore excludes logs/*.log but git cannot track an empty directory, so
without this file the directory does not exist in a clone. Found 2026-09-07 by
the first CI run this repository ever completed; it had been true for every
fresh clone all along, and was invisible locally because the directory already
existed untracked.
